NEXUS × TONYBOT — Unified Multi-Market Trading Platform

Technical Specification & Implementation Document (v1.0)

Scope: Merge NEXUS (Binance Futures live engine) and TONYBOT (PySide6 GUI + strategy + backtest) into a single market-agnostic kernel with pluggable adapters for memecoins (Solana), Polymarket (prediction market), and perpetual futures (Binance). Add a self-evolving AI layer on free tiers, run a 3-week shadow-trading demo with P&L monitoring, then gate real money behind go/no-go criteria. Sports/event markets are a future expansion, not part of v1.0.

Primary focus for v1.0: Memecoins + Polymarket. Perps are maintained and used as the "stable baseline" for validating the kernel. Sports/event expansion is Phase 6.

---

1. Executive Summary

1.1 What we are building

A single trading system where three fundamentally different markets are treated as notional exposure objects behind one interface. The kernel does not know what a "share" or a "contract" is—it knows USD notional, side, and a risk gate. Each market is an adapter.

1.2 Why not just merge the repos

NEXUS is a live execution engine (signed Binance requests, order lifecycle, SQLite journal, Telegram approval). TONYBOT is a strategy and research platform (GUI, indicators, regime classifier, backtester, ML ensemble, PDF reports). Copying files together produces two half-systems fighting for the main loop. The correct merge is:

· Kernel ← NEXUS's order_lifecycle.py, journal.py, risk_governor.py (generalized to USD notional).
· Strategy layer ← TONYBOT's regime_classifier.py, setup_scanner.py, signals.py, backtest/.
· UI ← TONYBOT's PySide6 dashboard, extended with a market selector tab per adapter.
· New ← three adapters, AI router, reflection loop, DSL engine, demo P&L tracker.

1.3 Non-negotiable constraints

Constraint Rule
Secrets Never in source, logs, Telegram, or issue comments. .env + .gitignore only.
Memecoin cap Hard $25 per trade during demo, independent of portfolio math.
Safety filter order Runs before risk kernel, not after.
Demo execution dry_run=True on all adapters for 3 weeks. Perps on Binance testnet.
AI failure AI is optional enrichment. If all providers fail, deterministic rules continue.
Real money One adapter at a time, after go/no-go. Polymarket first, perps last, memecoins last.

