4. Risk Kernel (single source of "no")

```python
# core/kernel/risk_engine.py
class RiskEngine:
    def __init__(self, cfg):
        self.max_total_exposure_pct = cfg.TOTAL_EXPOSURE_PCT        # 0.30
        self.market_caps = {
            Market.PERP:       0.15,
            Market.POLYMARKET: 0.10,
            Market.MEMECOIN:   0.05,
        }
        self.max_daily_loss_pct     = cfg.DAILY_LOSS_PCT            # 0.02
        self.max_drawdown_pct       = cfg.MAX_DRAWDOWN_PCT          # 0.15
        self.hard_caps_usd = {
            Market.MEMECOIN:   cfg.MEME_HARD_CAP_USD,               # 25
            Market.POLYMARKET: cfg.POLY_HARD_CAP_USD,               # 100
            Market.PERP:       cfg.PERP_HARD_CAP_USD,               # 500
        }

    async def gate(self, q: Quote) -> tuple[bool, str]:
        capital = await self.portfolio.total_capital_usd()
        total   = await self.portfolio.total_exposure_usd()

        if q.notional_usd > self.hard_caps_usd[q.adapter]:
            return False, "hard_cap_exceeded"

        if total + q.notional_usd > capital * self.max_total_exposure_pct:
            return False, "total_exposure_cap"

        mkt = await self.portfolio.market_exposure_usd(q.adapter)
        if mkt + q.notional_usd > capital * self.market_caps[q.adapter]:
            return False, "market_cap_exceeded"

        if await self.journal.daily_loss_pct() >= self.max_daily_loss_pct:
            return False, "daily_loss_breaker"

        if await self.journal.drawdown_pct() >= self.max_drawdown_pct:
            return False, "drawdown_breaker"

        return True, "approved"
```

Additional gate for perps only: funding-cost budget. A funding_watch coroutine polls every 60s; if projected daily funding cost on open positions exceeds FUNDING_BUDGET_USD, new entries are blocked with reason funding_budget.

Additional gate for memecoins: the safety filter result must be passed on the same Quote.metadata["safety"] object. The risk engine checks this field before anything else.

