6. Strategy DSL

6.1 Why DSL

Free-tier LLMs cannot reliably write Python trading code. They can reliably edit YAML parameters within a known schema. The DSL is the boundary: LLM proposes DSL changes, kernel compiles and backtests, only approved versions run live.

6.2 Schema (Pydantic)

```python
# core/strategy/dsl/schema.py
class Trigger(BaseModel):
    indicator: Literal["rsi", "macd", "volume_spike", "price_above_ema",
                       "bb_breakout", "prob_deviation", "time_to_resolution"]
    params: dict
    condition: str          # e.g. "< 30", "> 1.5", "abs() > 0.08"

class Guard(BaseModel):
    name: Literal["safety_filter", "max_notional_usd", "regime",
                  "liquidity_min_usd", "funding_budget"]
    params: dict

class Exit(BaseModel):
    stop_loss: dict | None
    take_profit: dict | None
    timeout_minutes: int | None

class StrategyDSL(BaseModel):
    id: str
    market: Literal["perp_binance", "polymarket", "solana_memecoin"]
    triggers: list[Trigger]
    guards: list[Guard]
    exit: Exit
    params: dict[str, float]   # tunable parameters, ranges declared
    param_ranges: dict[str, tuple[float, float]]
```

6.3 Compiler and validator

compiler.py produces a callable evaluate(context) -> Signal | None. validator.py enforces:

1. Every param key has a matching param_range.
2. Every Trigger.indicator is implemented for that market (Polymarket has no RSI).
3. Guards include safety_filter for solana_memecoin.
4. max_notional_usd guard present and ≤ hard cap.

A DSL that fails validation cannot be loaded. This is the safety boundary against LLM mutation drift.

6.4 Backtest gate for every version

Any new strategy_versions row from reflector must pass:

· Out-of-sample window ≥ 90 days.
· Win rate ≥ baseline − 3 percentage points, OR Sharpe improvement ≥ 0.15.
· Max drawdown ≤ current version + 20% relative.

Failing rows stay approved=0 and are never loaded by the live engine.

