Final Advice

You want "perfection," but the path to perfection is not to let the AI learn everything at once. It is to make the AI learn one thing at a time: first let it learn to reject bad trades (the fine-tuned reviewer), then let it learn to adjust parameters (the reflection loop), and finally consider letting it propose new strategy logic (the DSL mutation loop). Each step must be validated by backtest + shadow run before proceeding to the next. TradePool's RL training also started from 50 steps and a reward of 0.15, slowly climbing up. Your system should do the same.